# x = 7 in the A-field. (MOV x (Dir -1)) moves x's value into the B-field of the cell before the
# MOV (cell 2): beside a value, a cell is its B-field (MOV.AB), DAT #0, #7. Before the cell rule the
# ICWS'94 default .I copied the whole cell (DAT #7, #0).
golden: bbctests/examples/mixed_operand_field.bbc
cell 2 2 DAT.F #0, #7
